---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, AUTHORS } from '../data/site';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Calc from '../components/Calc.astro';
const faq = [];
const toc = [{ id: 'mission', label: 'Why this site exists' }, { id: 'covers', label: 'What we cover' }, { id: 'method', label: 'How we verify information' }, { id: 'calculators', label: 'How our calculators work' }, { id: 'corrections', label: 'Corrections' }, { id: 'independence', label: 'Independence and advertising' }, { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' }];
const related = ["editorial-policy", "contact-us"];
---

<SiteLayout title="About 8PayCommission: Independent 8th Pay Commission Guides" description="About 8PayCommission, an independent publisher of 8th Pay Commission guides and calculators. Our mission, sources, verification method and advertising policy." slug="about-us" h1="About 8PayCommission" lead="An independent site explaining the 8th Pay Commission." faq={faq} toc={toc} related={related} pageType="info" breadcrumbLabel="About Us">

<p>8PayCommission is an independent website that explains the 8th Central Pay Commission in plain language and provides calculators for central government employees and pensioners. We are not part of the Government of India, the Ministry of Finance or the commission.</p>
<h2 id="mission">Why this site exists</h2>
<p>Pay commission news is full of large numbers that are not official. A headline may promise a 100% raise, but the commission has not announced a fitment factor. Our aim is to show what is confirmed, what is only projected and what each case means in rupees for your pay level, so you can plan without relying on rumours.</p>
<h2 id="covers">What we cover</h2>
<ul>
<li>Verified updates on the commission, its timeline, consultations and Dearness Allowance.</li>
<li>Calculators for salary, arrears, pension, gratuity and allowances, plus pay matrix tables for all 18 levels.</li>
<li>Explainers on the fitment factor, DA merger, HRA, MACP, UPS and NPS, written for employees and pensioners.</li>
<li>Hindi pages on the topics people ask about most.</li>
</ul>
{AUTHORS.length > 0 && (<><h2 id="team">Who writes this site</h2>{AUTHORS.map((a) => (<div class="author"><h3>{a.name}</h3><p><strong>{a.role}</strong></p><p>{a.bio}</p></div>))}</>)}
<h2 id="method">How we verify information</h2>
<p>We rely on Cabinet and PIB statements, Finance Ministry and DoPT orders, replies in Parliament, the Labour Bureau's monthly index releases and the commission's own portal at 8cpc.gov.in. News reports are used only to find a story, then checked against an official source or marked as a press report. Each page shows when it was last updated, and projections are always labelled as projections. Read the full <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.</p>
<h2 id="calculators">How our calculators work</h2>
<p>Pay figures follow the 7th CPC pay matrix: entry pay for each level, a 3% yearly increment rounded to the nearest Rs 100, and Dearness Allowance at the current rate. For the 8th CPC we do not guess an outcome. We multiply today's basic pay by clearly labelled fitment scenarios (1.92, 2.28, 2.57 and 2.86) and show the result as an illustration. All calculations run in your browser, and the numbers you type are not sent to our servers.</p>
<h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
<p>If you find an error, tell us with the page address and an official source. We correct confirmed mistakes promptly and note material changes on the page.</p>
<h2 id="independence">Independence and advertising</h2>
<p>We are funded by advertising. Ads never influence what we publish, and we do not accept payment to promote a view about the commission. See our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> for how advertising cookies work.</p>
<h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
<p>Write to us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> for corrections, questions or feedback. See the <a href="/contact-us/">contact page</a>.</p>

</SiteLayout>
